Optimistic UI update without rollback on error: the comment is removed from local state before the API call completes. If the API call fails (empty catch on line 81), the comment disappears from the UI but still exists on the backend, creating inconsistency. Consider implementing rollback logic on error.
```suggestion
      let deletedComment: Comment | undefined;
      setComments(prev => {
        const index = prev.findIndex(c => c.id === commentId);
        if (index === -1) {
          return prev;
        }
        deletedComment = prev[index];
        return prev.filter(c => c.id !== commentId);
      });
      if (dataSource) {
        try {
          await dataSource.delete('sys_comment', commentId);
        } catch {
          if (deletedComment) {
            // Roll back optimistic update on error
            setComments(prev => {
              const exists = prev.some(c => c.id === deletedComment!.id);
              return exists ? prev : [...prev, deletedComment!];
            });
          }
        }
```
